================================================================================
 corpus/ — third-party music, included as test vectors
================================================================================

The `.v2m` files in this directory are NOT public domain and are NOT covered by
the repository's CC0 dedication (see ../LICENSE).

WHAT THEY ARE
    Each file is a genuine V2M song carved unmodified from the executable of an
    original, freely-distributed Farbrausch / .theprodukkt demo release (e.g.
    .the .product, flybye, mark&sweep, candytron, .kkrieger, …). Per-song source
    release and SHA-256 provenance are documented in embedded/PROVENANCE.md.

WHY THEY ARE HERE
    They serve a single technical purpose: ground-truth test vectors for this
    player's determinism gate (test/check.py) and the fidelity/oracle work
    documented in docs/ACCURACY.md. The player is validated by rendering these
    genuine songs and comparing against reference renders from the original
    engines. They are not provided for redistribution as music.

RIGHTS
    These compositions remain the property of their original authors. No
    copyright or other rights are claimed over them by this repository, and they
    are NOT relicensed. They are reproduced here under no license grant beyond
    the fact that the source demos were released for free public distribution.

REMOVAL
    If you are a rights holder (artist or group) and would prefer a song not be
    redistributed here, please open an issue or contact the maintainer. It will
    be removed promptly, no questions asked.

REPRODUCING THE CORPUS YOURSELF
    The corpus is fully reproducible from the original demo releases. See
    embedded/PROVENANCE.md for each source archive, its SHA-256, and the carve
    procedure, so the test vectors can be regenerated rather than redistributed.
